    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d388">

                <pb facs="0552" n="458" sameAs="frus:frus1924v02/pg458"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">881.00/927: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Italy</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Fletcher</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Rome</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1924-06-07T13:00:00+01:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 7, 1924—1
                                p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received 7:22 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>110. Your 72, June 4, 5 p.m. Foreign Office states that the attitude of the
                    Italian Government on the subject has not been formulated in detail but that
                    they are not disposed to adhere to the convention without reservations. They
                    desire to act in complete accord in this matter with us and have promised to
                    communicate to me their proposed reply before sending it with this end in view.
                    Is this satisfactory?</p>
                <p>I was asked what our attitude would be and replied that I had no definite
                    instructions but explained the attitude of the Department <pb facs="0553"
                        n="459" xml:id="pg459"/> during the course of the negotiations as set out in
                    the enclosures to Department’s instruction number 408, October 1923<anchor n="8"
                        xml:id="d388-f1"/> and page 12 of confidential monthly political report for
                    December 1923.<anchor n="9" xml:id="d388-f2"/></p>
                <p>Please instruct.<anchor n="10" xml:id="d388-f3"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Fletcher</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
